{"authored" [{"question" "q-80430" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14053940/assets/d7db51d6af763e8853f815feb6e74b88d0ca9a19e79c42b3a42da4e8b088f93c.png)\n\nConsider the region $D$ shown above. If \n\n$$\nf(x,y)={\\begin{aligned}x+y, & (x,y)\\in R\\cap D \\\\ 0, & (x,y)\\in R∖D\\end{aligned}\\,\\text{and}\\,{∬}_{D}(x+y)\\,\\text{d}A={∬}_{R}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}A,\n$$\n\nRequire $D\\subseteq R$, so the rectangle contains the entire region. Which of the following could be the definition of the rectangular domain $R?$\n\n- $R=[-2,2]\\times [-1,1]$\n- $R=[0,2]\\times [-2,2]$\n- $R=[-2,2]\\times [-2,2]$" "category" "mathematical_correction" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/mathematical-corrections/q-80430/review.json" "file_sha256" "013747154102fb480ba50a0ce0dcddc44e59e7fde57b39644e78b1d6547bc8e0" "transaction" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/mathematical-corrections/q-80430/transaction.edn" "transaction_sha256" "a2421cd6717dc0f82de7aa6a0a8456b75996c62ef9a82913d4be576802f98a7a" "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/mathematical-corrections/q-80430/verification.json" "basis" 1799 "rationale" "Make the verified containing-region interpretation explicit in the study request. The prompt now requires D subset R and the worked solution checks each rectangle against the actual ellipse or displayed domain. Zero extension on a containing rectangle preserves the integral. Keys and complete answer fields remain unchanged; original source, grades and interpretations remain preserved. Equality for a particular integrand alone is not a general containment criterion, illustrated decisively by q129666 odd-in-x cancellation."} {"question" "q-80430" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The displayed region has points above $y=1$, so rectangle I, whose vertical range is $[-1,1]$, does not contain all of $D$. The region also has points with $x<0$, so rectangle II, whose horizontal range is $[0,2]$, does not contain all of $D$. The entire drawn region lies in rectangle III, $[-2,2]\\times[-2,2]$.\n\nFor rectangle III, $f=x+y$ on $D$ and is zero on $R\\setminus D$. Therefore $\\iint_R f\\,dA=\\iint_D(x+y)\\,dA$. Only III meets the explicit containment requirement, giving \"III only\"." "category" "mathematical_correction" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/mathematical-corrections/q-80430/review.json" "file_sha256" "013747154102fb480ba50a0ce0dcddc44e59e7fde57b39644e78b1d6547bc8e0" "transaction" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/mathematical-corrections/q-80430/transaction.edn" "transaction_sha256" "a2421cd6717dc0f82de7aa6a0a8456b75996c62ef9a82913d4be576802f98a7a" "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/mathematical-corrections/q-80430/verification.json" "basis" 1799 "rationale" "Make the verified containing-region interpretation explicit in the study request. The prompt now requires D subset R and the worked solution checks each rectangle against the actual ellipse or displayed domain. Zero extension on a containing rectangle preserves the integral. Keys and complete answer fields remain unchanged; original source, grades and interpretations remain preserved. Equality for a particular integrand alone is not a general containment criterion, illustrated decisively by q129666 odd-in-x cancellation."} {"question" "q-80430" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "III only"] "category" "mathematical_correction" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/mathematical-corrections/q-80430/review.json" "file_sha256" "013747154102fb480ba50a0ce0dcddc44e59e7fde57b39644e78b1d6547bc8e0" "transaction" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/mathematical-corrections/